ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20555, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NTDHciyqvkDk1V4jS7oZpA", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20555, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GZfC4mvQcXhsHcwEszzdUh", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20855, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GZfC4mvQcXhsHcwEszzdUh", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20855, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GZfC4mvQcXhsHcwEszzdUh", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25497, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_011BpsyK4EUhPe7m5e2MYD6f", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 went out to all production regions, checkout-api started failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the service on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator partial-rollout error, and keep v2.3.1 from being redeployed until it is fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56097, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011BpsyK4EUhPe7m5e2MYD6f", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56097, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011BpsyK4EUhPe7m5e2MYD6f", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57646, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012tbuVmPYzVNyuN2oHRZ1wn", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57946, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012tbuVmPYzVNyuN2oHRZ1wn", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57946, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012tbuVmPYzVNyuN2oHRZ1wn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63348, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-good version is safe to repeat, so I tried once more and it finished in all regions. checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api). It describes the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and the follow-ups. The request timed out, but I checked the incident list and it had been created, so I didn't send it again and there's no duplicate page.\n\nThe incident lists three follow-ups:\n- Find out why v2.3.1 failed. Its release candidate was also unhealthy in staging.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback.\n- Don't redeploy v2.3.1 until it's fixed. Since it has never been healthy in production, redeploying it would need change-manager approval anyway.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JWRWGN9xQL5k5kDun8HVJh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WyXXnc2PwnNJV7RyLryTTy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DnGmgF1ZhSMVpxBkcENFSx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PAPw2qh4k9AKN1ijnfnrfx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy version again is safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GFeh7hWiEQ9qifJG7aKqB6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NTDHciyqvkDk1V4jS7oZpA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GZfC4mvQcXhsHcwEszzdUh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011BpsyK4EUhPe7m5e2MYD6f", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 went out to all production regions, checkout-api started failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the service on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator partial-rollout error, and keep v2.3.1 from being redeployed until it is fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_012tbuVmPYzVNyuN2oHRZ1wn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-good version is safe to repeat, so I tried once more and it finished in all regions. checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api). It describes the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and the follow-ups. The request timed out, but I checked the incident list and it had been created, so I didn't send it again and there's no duplicate page.\n\nThe incident lists three follow-ups:\n- Find out why v2.3.1 failed. Its release candidate was also unhealthy in staging.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback.\n- Don't redeploy v2.3.1 until it's fixed. Since it has never been healthy in production, redeploying it would need change-manager approval anyway.", "type": "text"}]}]}